to put it there  now that still creates its own problem  because it can result in representation  that is token and easily removed a  couple of scant lines of dialogue that  are easy to cut out without massively  affecting the story so you don't end up  with a bohemian rhapsody situation but  the fact that bohemian rhapsody got a  release in china means that  they are willing to take it out even  when it's thoroughly integrated into the  story so i would still say that's not  really a good excuse either but again  i've said in the past i would rather  have some form of representation even if  it's token and needs work it needs to be  better than to have none whatsoever  because if there's some representation  doesn't mean i'll be happy about it if  if it's bad or if it is overly token but  it's much easier to to work on and fix  and adjust and progress a thing that  exists  then something that isn't even there  getting the representation there at all  is a step we are still working on  and  the fact that sometimes that gets erased  when it gets moved to other countries or  gets brought over here  is  absolutely infuriating  and i kind of needed to get it off my  chest a bit  what are your thoughts on this  any other uh particularly juicy examples  you care to cite i'm sure there are many  i missed whatever your thoughts are drop  something down the comments let's talk  about it  there's a bunch of other stuff to do  like share subscribe i have a patreon  that's how i pay my bills uh rewards for  every tier also there's youtube  memberships if you'd rather go that way  but um  i'm not going to put that much pressure  on you  because  at the end of the day  you are the council  i only run the meetings and until next  time this council  is adjourned  [Music]  this video wouldn't have been possible  without the support of my patrons and i  want to give special thanks to jared  boyce  mj the doctor tracy scrabbit vincent  paul bartolucci kailyn schwartz edelon  robin moore ross schultz and shayla  gordon  thanks so much  [Music]  um  [Music]  hmm  [Music]
 

